  "scope_notes": "The PR adds a major new fuzz target (`p2p_1p1c_liveness.cpp`) of over 500 lines that drives a real `PeerManager` end-to-end to verify transaction liveness invariants.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Dropped earlier changes that introduced a dedicated txid cache for nonstandard-input rejections and re-requested missing parents on failed orphan retry; focused the patch set specifically on the peer handover, reject filter handling of conflicts, orphan retention on package feerate failure, and typed announcements forgetting in TxRequestTracker.",
  "card": "This PR fixes several liveness and pinning vulnerabilities in 1-parent-1-child package relay and adds an end-to-end fuzz target verifying bounded CPFP relay propagation against adversarial peers. Adversarial or disconnecting peers could prevent CPFP transactions from reaching the mempool by stranding orphans when assigned announcers disconnect, poisoning reject filters using witnessless copies of known transactions, purging orphans globally on package feerate failures caused by malleated parents, or wiping pending orphan parent requests when txid equals wtxid. The patch reassigns orphan reconsideration upon announcer eviction, excludes conflict results from reject filters, keeps orphans on reconsiderable package errors, and implements typed forgetting in TxRequestTracker. It depends on PR 36437.",
